WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.340
Cortes began heap leaching 2 million tons of run of mine gold or in 1971 without milling

00:00:05.340 --> 00:00:11.480
it first. This is First Principles Daily, episode 175. At the Cortes mine in Nevada,

00:00:11.900 --> 00:00:16.880
the operators set that low grade ore on asphalt pads and trickle dilute cyanide solution

00:00:16.880 --> 00:00:21.680
through the pile. The grinding step dropped out of the root for material that would otherwise

00:00:21.680 --> 00:00:27.720
have stayed uneconomic. George M. Potter of the US Bureau of Mines had already run the laboratory

00:00:27.720 --> 00:00:33.229
and pilot work that made the shift possible. Through the late 1960s, the conventional

00:00:33.229 --> 00:00:38.649
route still began with crushing, then fine grinding in mills so cyanide could reach the metal

00:00:38.649 --> 00:00:44.769
particles inside agitated tanks. Mines had long reduced ore to a fine powder so cyanide

00:00:44.769 --> 00:00:50.209
could dissolve the gold while the solids hung in suspension. That circuit needed ball or

00:00:50.209 --> 00:00:55.769
rod mills, thickeners, and large volumes of water and power. Only higher grade material

00:00:55.769 --> 00:01:01.149
paid for those costs. Anything below roughly a tenth of an ounce per ton was left in the ground

00:01:01.149 --> 00:01:06.669
or stockpiled. The standing assumption was that physical liberation of the gold particles had to

00:01:06.669 --> 00:01:12.649
come before chemical attack. Decades of milling practice had handed that assumption down, and marginal

00:01:12.649 --> 00:01:18.529
deposits rarely got a fresh look. Carlin Gold mining company still ran its main ore through a full

00:01:18.529 --> 00:01:24.429
mill circuit, even while it tested heap methods on lower-grade open-pit material. Capital locked

00:01:24.429 --> 00:01:28.849
in the grinding equipment and the energy that equipment burned, set a practical floor

00:01:28.849 --> 00:01:31.109
conventional operations could not get under.

00:01:31.669 --> 00:01:37.429
Each stage of size reduction added motors, liners, pumps, and classifiers that had to be maintained

00:01:37.429 --> 00:01:38.909
and powered without a break.

00:01:39.489 --> 00:01:44.429
Fine particles needed careful handling so dust did not walk off and so the pulp stayed

00:01:44.429 --> 00:01:46.249
at the right density for agitation.

00:01:46.849 --> 00:01:51.969
Because the entire or mass moved through those steps, even a modest daily tonnage multiplied

00:01:51.969 --> 00:01:56.289
the installed horsepower and the volume of water that had to be clarified and recycled.

00:01:56.909 --> 00:02:00.309
Operators accepted the expense because past practice had shown

00:02:00.309 --> 00:02:05.589
Corsair Rock left too much gold locked inside unbroken pieces. The convention therefore

00:02:05.589 --> 00:02:10.329
carried the equipment list and the energy budget forward without retesting whether every size

00:02:10.329 --> 00:02:16.669
reduction stage was still necessary once the goal was simply to expose gold surfaces to dilute cyanide.

00:02:16.669 --> 00:02:20.458
Bureau of Mine's metallurgists asked a different question.

00:02:20.958 --> 00:02:25.678
What minimum physical work was actually required to bring cyanide into contact with the gold.

00:02:26.298 --> 00:02:31.138
Laboratory tests on Cortez samples showed that ore crushed only to 3-quarter inch size

00:02:31.498 --> 00:02:36.258
and stacked in heaps still released about 70% of its gold when leached for seven days

00:02:36.258 --> 00:02:38.498
with dilute sodium cyanide solution.

00:02:39.258 --> 00:02:42.758
Pilot heaps at Cortez confirmed that result at larger scale.

00:02:42.758 --> 00:02:48.458
mine-manager Don Duncan then put run of mine cut off or unprepared pads no

00:02:48.458 --> 00:02:52.678
ball mills no classifiers and no counter-current decantations circuit were

00:02:52.678 --> 00:02:57.498
built for that tonnage the bureau sources record labor equipment and reagent

00:02:57.498 --> 00:03:01.798
quantities for the heap operation they do not report the dollar cost of the

00:03:01.798 --> 00:03:05.678
conventional milling route and they do not report the precise reagent and

00:03:05.678 --> 00:03:10.138
pumping energy that would constitute a raw material floor the magic wand

00:03:10.138 --> 00:03:14.958
number is what the finished thing would cost if you paid only for the raw materials. Here,

00:03:15.138 --> 00:03:19.778
the cyanide and the energy to move solution through rock, with every mill and thickener

00:03:19.778 --> 00:03:24.778
waived away. Without those paired figures, there is no floor to divide a finished price by,

00:03:25.258 --> 00:03:30.578
so the first principles ratio cannot be calculated from the record. That is a gap in the measurement,

00:03:30.818 --> 00:03:36.098
not a verdict on the people who built either circuit. What the sources do show is the removal of

00:03:36.098 --> 00:03:40.038
one entire class of equipment and the energy and maintenance that class carried.

00:03:40.638 --> 00:03:44.978
The key test was whether solution could percolate through the corsa fragments fast enough

00:03:44.978 --> 00:03:48.718
to reach most of the exposed gold surfaces inside a practical time.

00:03:49.438 --> 00:03:53.858
Holding the ore at a three quarter inch top size meant the operators never paid the power

00:03:53.858 --> 00:03:57.998
draw of the final grinding stages that would have turned the rock into a slurry.

00:03:58.638 --> 00:04:03.038
They also never paid the capital cost of the thickeners and filters that normally separate

00:04:03.038 --> 00:04:07.778
pregnant solution from finely ground solids. Recovery sat below what a full

00:04:07.778 --> 00:04:12.338
mill circuit could achieve on the same ore. The capital that was not spent is what

00:04:12.338 --> 00:04:16.558
let the mind treat material that would otherwise have stayed in the ground. One

00:04:16.558 --> 00:04:20.218
obvious objection is that skipping fine grinding must leave some gold

00:04:20.218 --> 00:04:24.798
particles coated or enclosed. The sources acknowledge that heap leaching works

00:04:24.798 --> 00:04:29.558
best on oxidized non refractory ores, where the gold is already accessible

00:04:29.558 --> 00:04:34.398
along fractures. Another objection is that solution losses or channeling could

00:04:34.398 --> 00:04:38.638
waste reagent. The Bureau reports note that operators learned to manage

00:04:38.638 --> 00:04:43.098
percolation by building the heaps properly and by adding agglomeration steps

00:04:43.098 --> 00:04:47.278
when fines were present. The redesign therefore worked because the OR at

00:04:47.278 --> 00:04:51.178
Cortez already met the physical condition that allowed direct contact without

00:04:51.178 --> 00:04:55.878
prior ultra fine size reduction. The decision sequence ran from laboratory

00:04:55.878 --> 00:05:00.978
territory confirmation, to pilot heaps, to full-scale placement, and each step took another

00:05:00.978 --> 00:05:05.418
piece out of the inherited milling train instead of copying that train at a smaller scale.

00:05:06.317 --> 00:05:10.897
Heap leaching at Carlin and Cortez brought previously sub-economic ore into production

00:05:10.897 --> 00:05:14.717
with far lower installed capital than a new mill circuit would have required.

00:05:15.317 --> 00:05:19.217
The material that moved was the 0.07 ounce per ton ore.

00:05:19.717 --> 00:05:24.397
The method spread to other low-grade deposits in the 1970s because the capital barrier

00:05:24.397 --> 00:05:24.937
had dropped.

00:05:24.937 --> 00:05:30.237
It could not treat refractory sulfide ores that still needed roasting or pressure oxidation,

00:05:30.777 --> 00:05:35.237
and solution losses or poor percolation remained operational problems at some sites.

00:05:35.957 --> 00:05:40.657
Reagent consumption and pumping energy still set a physical floor, but the sources give

00:05:40.657 --> 00:05:42.077
no measured value for it.

00:05:42.537 --> 00:05:47.577
Suitable pad foundations and solution containment added cost of their own, though those costs

00:05:47.577 --> 00:05:50.017
were smaller than the grinding plant that was avoided.

00:05:50.017 --> 00:05:54.277
Over time, the industry added carbon adsorption and other refinements.

00:05:54.657 --> 00:05:59.157
The core simplification, skipping fine grinding for suitable ores, stayed in place.

00:05:59.737 --> 00:06:04.777
The gold still locked inside unbroken fragments is the gap that remains, and no amount of

00:06:04.777 --> 00:06:08.957
heap redesign recovers that gold without bringing some form of size reduction back.

00:06:09.937 --> 00:06:14.117
When the chemical reaction can occur without first reducing the entire mass to powder,

00:06:14.617 --> 00:06:18.497
the equipment that performed that reduction becomes optional rather than obligatory.

00:06:18.497 --> 00:06:23.757
The same logic applies wherever an intermediate physical step is retained only because past

00:06:23.757 --> 00:06:25.777
practice treated it as unavoidable.

00:06:26.257 --> 00:06:31.037
Which other mineral or chemical processes still carry an inherited grinding or size reduction

00:06:31.037 --> 00:06:34.597
stage that a direct contact test would show is unnecessary.

